  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The only way in",
      "items": [
        "The gate checks the garden's Access JWT on every request and WebSocket, the garden Origin on upgrades, and Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin for anything but a read",
        "It passes only listed headers: the editor never sees the Access token or cookies, and never sets a cookie or COOP",
        "Only the workbench and code-server's own frames load as pages; everything else is nosniff with CSP sandbox",
        "The editor listens only on editor.sock; only the gate (ro) and the editor mount code-server-sock"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not connected",
      "items": [
        "The editor and the shell are not on the stack's default network: no route to the app-server, the BFF, the vault, Gmail triggers or garden",
        "No code editor service opens a connection to the app-server or the BFF or starts a turn",
        "code-exec is internal and holds only the editor and the shell; only the shell is on code-egress"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "As strong as an agent",
      "items": [
        "Terminals (exec-shell) and Source Control's git (shell-git) run over SSH in the shell, through agent-env",
        "The shell is the app-server's image with the workspaces and /opt/agent-tools mounted read-write, like the agents'",
        "The editor shares the garden origin with the vault and Gmail triggers, so it stays in Restricted Mode and runs nothing from the workspaces"
      ]
    }
  ]
